  "content": {
    "id": "p44-q7",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "A thickshake is $\\$2$ more than a fruit juice.\nIf 3 thickshakes and 5 fruit juices cost $\\$30$, determine their individual prices.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Fruit juice: $\\$3$; thickshake: $\\$5$.",
      "worked": "Let $t$ be the price of a thickshake and $j$ be the price of a fruit juice, in dollars.\n$$\\begin{align*}t&=j+2\\quad\\text{(1)}\\\\3t+5j&=30\\quad\\text{(2)}\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute (1) into (2).\n$$\\begin{align*}3(j+2)+5j&=30\\\\8j+6&=30\\\\8j&=24\\\\j&=3\\\\t&=3+2\\\\t&=5\\end{align*}$$\nA fruit juice costs $\\$3$ and a thickshake costs $\\$5$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 66
  },
